# ── Swift half ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.build/
.DS_Store
DerivedData/
*.xcuserdata/
*.xcworkspace/
*.xcodeproj/
*.log

# ── Server half (server/, added by SONNY-126) ────────────────────────────────
# Dependencies and build output. Both are reproducible from the lockfile and the
# source, and node_modules in particular is large enough to make every diff unreadable.
node_modules/
server/dist/
server/coverage/
server/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment files. This is the line that matters most in this file: provider
# credentials are the entire reason the backend exists, and `.env` is the one place a
# real key is genuinely likely to be typed. `server/.env.example` is committed and
# carries placeholders only; every other .env is ignored, including per-environment
# ones, so a file named after staging or production cannot slip in either.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
server/.env
server/.env.*
!server/.env.example

# Vendor CLI state. Written into the working tree by deploy tooling; carries account
# and organisation identifiers rather than tokens, and belongs to nobody's history.
# (SONNY-125 caught these staged twice; this is the repo-wide version of the ignore
# that branch could only add inside scripts/host-probe/.)
.wrangler/
**/.wrangler/
.temp/
**/supabase/.temp/

# ── Founder-only reference doc, not part of the repo's tracked history ───────
docs/sonny-v1-product-overview.md
